  "question": {
    "text": "<p>A pole is vertically submerged in swimming pool, such that it gives a length of shadow <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>15</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> within water when sunlight is incident at an angle of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>30</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math> with the surface of water. If swimming pool is filled to a height of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>,</mo></math> then the height of the pole above the water surface in centimeters is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mo>.</mo></math></p>"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "50",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p><img src=\"assets\\st0101_2d6d61f8b3da.png\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 195px;\" /></p><p>Let angle&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi><mi>A</mi><mi>C</mi></math>&nbsp;is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#952;</mi></math>.</p><p>Applying Snell&#39;s law at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>E</mi></math>, we get&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mi>sin</mi><mn>60</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mi>sin</mi><mi>&#952;</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>sin</mi><mi>&#952;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mrow><mn>8</mn></mfrac><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>tan</mi><mi>&#952;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mi>&#952;</mi></mrow><msqrt><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mi>&#952;</mi></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></msqrt></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mrow><msqrt><mn>37</mn></msqrt></mfrac></math></p><p>Now,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mi>tan</mi><mi>&#952;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>28</mn></math></p><p>Then,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>15</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>86</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math></p><p>Required value,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>D</mi><mi>F</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>tan</mi><mn>30</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5015</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#8776;</mo><mn>50</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math></p></blockquote>"
  }
}